questions.q:
In a food web:
grass is eaten by rabbits and grasshoppers;
grasshoppers are eaten by frogs;
frogs are eaten by snakes;
rabbits are eaten by foxes and snakes.
(a) Name one primary consumer. [1]
(b) Name the organism that is both a secondary consumer and a tertiary consumer. [1]

In a food web:
grass is eaten by rabbits and grasshoppers;
grasshoppers are eaten by frogs;
frogs are eaten by snakes;
rabbits are eaten by foxes and snakes.
A foreign species of lizard that eats only grasshoppers is introduced into the area. It has no predators.
Suggest and explain the effects of introducing this lizard on the populations of two other organisms in the food web.
